        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "Group 2 nitrates decompose to the metal oxide, nitrogen dioxide and oxygen: 2M(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> → 2MO + 4NO<sub>2</sub> + O<sub>2</sub>. So each mole of nitrate releases 2 mol NO<sub>2</sub> + 0.5 mol O<sub>2</sub> = 2 × 46.0 + 0.5 × 32.0 = 108.0 g of gas, whatever the metal.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:10.1(3)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Mass of gas ÷ mass of nitrate = 1.53 ÷ 3.00 = 0.510 = 108.0 ÷ M<sub>r</sub>, so M<sub>r</sub> = 108.0 ÷ 0.510 = 212. M<sub>r</sub>(M(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>) = A<sub>r</sub>(M) + 124.0, so A<sub>r</sub>(M) ≈ 88, which is strontium (87.6, Sr(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> = 211.6).",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:2.4(1)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "optionAnalysis": [
            {
              "key": "A",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "Be(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> has M<sub>r</sub> = 133.0; 3.00 g would give 3.00 × 108.0/133.0 = 2.44 g of gas."
            },
            {
              "key": "B",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "Ca(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> has M<sub>r</sub> = 164.1; 3.00 g would give 1.97 g of gas."
            },
            {
              "key": "C",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "Mg(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> has M<sub>r</sub> = 148.3; 3.00 g would give 2.18 g of gas."
            },
            {
              "key": "D",
              "correct": true,
              "text": "Correct. Sr(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> has M<sub>r</sub> = 211.6; 3.00 g gives 3.00 × 108.0/211.6 = 1.53 g of gas."
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Equation: M(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> → MO + 2NO<sub>2</sub> + ½O<sub>2</sub>.",
            "Gas per mole of nitrate = 92.0 + 16.0 = 108.0 g.",
            "M<sub>r</sub> of nitrate = 108.0 × 3.00 ÷ 1.53 = 212.",
            "A<sub>r</sub>(M) = 212 − 124 = 88, so M is strontium."
          ],
